{"school":{"dbn":"24Q311","name":"Corona Arts & Sciences Academy","boro":"Queens","district":"24","district_label":"District 24","report_type":"EMS","report_types":"EMS","school_type":"Middle","grades":"6 to 8","status":"open","enrollment":764,"enrollment_year":"2024-25","address":"98-11 44TH AVENUE, QUEENS, NY 11368","phone":"332-262-2861","website":"www.CASA311.org","directory_url":"https://www.myschools.nyc/en/schools/middle-school/65929","accessibility":"Fully Accessible","overview":"Our instructional philosophy is built upon the belief that literacy is the life blood of education and embed reading and writing into all content areas. Equally as important, we believe that we have a responsibility to educate the whole child and provide many opportunities to enhance learning in a profound manner by taking learning beyond the walls of the classroom  Our Arts Elective Program lets students choose from a variety of Arts and Science courses, preparing them for specialized high schools and showcasing their work in Winter and Spring events. Our STEM program teaches students to tackle real-world challenges like scientists and engineers, building crucial problem-solving and critical thinking skills.  Our unique project-based learning (PBL) initiatives, including \"CASA Community Wednesdays\" (07:50 AM to 12:10 PM), give students the choice to engage in areas they are passionate about which include Social Justice, STEM, Community Service, Healthy Lifestyles, Financial Literacy, and Sustainability.  We foster strong partnerships among staff, students, and families to support our students' growth preparing their future. Our CREW Advisory program involves social-emotional learning, team-building activities, and student-led conferences. Families can opt students into our Dual Language program and at the end of 6th grade, families can choose an accelerated program for 7th and 8th grade.  CASA students can join our award-winning school band and debate team, participate in sports like our girls and boys basketball and volleyball teams, and our championship-winning co-ed futsal team. They can also use our wellness room, enjoy various after-school activities, attend Broadway plays, participate in their own plays, and be active in student government. We collaborate with NYC Outward Bound, Urban Advantage, and more.  As part of the Progressive Redesign Opportunity Schools for Excellence (PROSE) program, CASA has the flexibility to innovate in teaching methods and school design. We extend class periods, implement unique teacher evaluations, and focus on real-world problem-solving. This allows us to personalize learning for each student while maintaining high performance standards.  We prioritize admissions for students (52% of seats at CASA) from low-income households, those in temporary housing, and English Language Learners (ELLs), ensuring a diverse and inclusive learning environment. Join us at CASA, where we ignite a passion for learning and empower students to reach their fullest potential.","start_time":"07:50am","end_time":"02:41pm","languages":null,"subway":"7 to 103rd St","bus":"Q23, Q29, Q38, Q48, Q58, Q72","shared_building":"0","neighborhood":"Corona","latitude":40.745976,"longitude":-73.86501,"coordinate_source":"geocoded","first_year":"2015-16","last_year":"2024-25"},"series":{"attendance_inperson_k8_all":{"y":["2020-21"],"v":[0.958],"st":["ok"],"n":[437.0]},"attendance_k8_all":{"y":["2018-19","2019-20","2020-21","2021-22","2022-23","2023-24","2024-25"],"v":[0.959,0.952,0.895,0.916,0.925,0.939,0.932],"st":["ok","ok","ok","ok","ok","ok","ok"],"n":[790.0,793.0,765.0,835.0,874.0,825.0,821.0],"c":[null,null,null,null,null,1.0,0.908]},"attendance_remote_k8_all":{"y":["2020-21"],"v":[0.89],"st":["ok"],"n":[765.0]},"chronic_absent_ems_all":{"y":["2015-16","2016-17","2017-18","2018-19","2019-20","2020-21","2021-22","2022-23","2023-24","2024-25"],"v":[0.958,0.956,0.909,0.893,0.872,0.692,0.718,0.764,0.814,0.796],"st":["ok","ok","ok","ok","ok"